# Allowlist: the image gets only what the server runs and serves. Everything
# else in the build context (docs, tests, scripts, Terraform, agent files)
# stays out.
#
# Files are enumerated individually, not by directory (`!backend/`), because
# a directory-level allowlist re-includes EVERY file under that path by name
# — including an untracked local file (a stray secret, a half-finished edit)
# that was never committed. Enumerating exact files means an untracked file
# dropped into backend/, css/, or js/ is still caught by the leading `*` and
# never reaches the image, even if someone runs `docker build .` directly
# instead of the git-archive-based build in docs/aws-deployment.md.
#
# Keep this list in sync with `git ls-files backend css js server.py
# index.html LICENSE NOTICE`. A new tracked file that isn't added here is
# left out of the image (server.py fails to import it) rather than silently
# shipping an untracked one — a loud failure on build/boot, not a silent leak.
*
!server.py
!index.html
!LICENSE
!NOTICE
!backend/__init__.py
!backend/bom_cache.py
!backend/cid_manager.py
!backend/db.py
!backend/dtrack_client.py
!backend/extractor.py
!backend/gh_auth.py
!backend/github_client.py
!backend/github_sbom.py
!backend/log.py
!backend/mocker.py
!backend/ort_runner.py
!backend/package_extractor.py
!backend/pipeline.py
!backend/poetry_fallback.py
!backend/prelock.py
!backend/sandbox.py
!backend/sanitizer.py
!backend/secrets_loader.py
!backend/settings.py
!backend/task_queue.py
!css/styles.css
!js/api.js
!js/app.js
!js/package_search.js
!js/runs.js
!js/settings.js
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
